  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/CardMarks.tsx",
      "content": "Selecting another cell while a correction is dirty silently discards its price and reason. Changing `chosen` replaces the keyed `CellEditor`, while `MarkEntry` stores those values locally and clears its dirty report on unmount. `pagingHeld` only blocks page buttons, not cell selection. Preserve editors' correction state by key, or prevent/confirm selection changes until the correction is saved or cancelled. Add a test that enters a correction, selects another cell, and returns.",
      "existing_code": "        onChoose={setChosen}",
      "start_line": 324,
      "end_line": 324,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/CardMarks.tsx",
      "content": "A rejected price draft can be on a different page from the one currently displayed, since drafts persist across paging. Selecting its key opens the editor but does not change `MarksGrid`'s private page state; Missing prices exist only in the grid, so the requested input is absent and the focus effect does nothing. Reveal the rejected key's page before focusing its input, and cover rejection after navigating away from a drafted page.",
      "existing_code": "        setChosen(first.key);\n        setFocusField({ field: first.issue.field });",
      "start_line": 287,
      "end_line": 288,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/CardMarks.tsx",
      "content": "With persistent drafts across pages, users can enter more than 100 prices. In that case Save Marks remains enabled but this branch silently does nothing, with no explanation or recovery guidance. Display the limit and how many drafts must be cleared, or provide a supported way to save within the limit instead of silently returning.",
      "existing_code": "    if (prepared.kind === 'TooMany') return;",
      "start_line": 242,
      "end_line": 242,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
